part.text:
Fixed in `/workspace/app/product/page.tsx`.

**Problem:** The product page was blocking on `await getInventory()` before rendering any content, including the title `Premium Widget`.

**Solution:** I extracted the async data fetch into a separate `Inventory` component and wrapped it in React `Suspense`. Now the title renders immediately while the inventory data streams in asynchronously.

```tsx
// Before: title blocked until data loaded
export default async function ProductPage() {
  const inventory = await getInventory()  // blocks everything
  return <main><h1>Premium Widget</h1>...</main>
}

// After: title renders immediately, data streams in
export default function ProductPage() {
  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Premium Widget</h1>
      <Suspense fallback={<p>Loading inventory...</p>}>
        <Inventory />
      </Suspense>
    </main>
  )
}
```
